1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,977
Welcome, team.

2
00:00:02,477 --> 00:00:09,420
AI is changing every industry, and fast. It can speed up our work and keep our workflows consistent.

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:17,188
But you told us you have real questions about privacy, security and trust. That is exactly why we are here.

4
00:00:18,588 --> 00:00:22,117
We read every one of your responses, and four themes stood out.

5
00:00:22,617 --> 00:00:28,457
Privacy and security. Is our information, and our clients' information, safe?

6
00:00:28,957 --> 00:00:31,720
Accuracy. Can we trust what it tells us?

7
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:35,239
Authenticity. Will we lose our human touch?

8
00:00:35,739 --> 00:00:38,421
And balance. How much should we share with it?

9
00:00:39,821 --> 00:00:45,184
Here is one idea that makes everything simpler: treat Claude like a brand-new team member.

10
00:00:45,684 --> 00:00:52,116
You would not hand a new hire every password on day one. You would guide them, check their work, and stay in charge.

11
00:00:53,516 --> 00:00:57,301
First, protect. Know where your information goes.

12
00:00:57,801 --> 00:01:11,106
On a Team or Enterprise plan, Anthropic does not train its models on our conversations by default. On a personal account, a Model Improvement setting controls this, so check it, and stick to our approved work account.

13
00:01:11,606 --> 00:01:15,229
Claude reaches the internet only through features that are turned on.

14
00:01:15,729 --> 00:01:21,162
And connected apps, like Drive or Gmail, only show Claude what you can already see.

15
00:01:21,662 --> 00:01:26,248
So connect only what we need, and disconnect anything we stop using.

16
00:01:27,648 --> 00:01:29,529
Then use the traffic light.

17
00:01:30,029 --> 00:01:40,060
Red means never share: passwords and logins, API keys, full card or bank numbers, and Social Security or government ID numbers.

18
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:51,938
Yellow means ask first, and only in approved tools: client details, anything under a confidentiality agreement, and employee, payroll or medical records.

19
00:01:52,438 --> 00:01:57,383
Green means go ahead: your own drafts, public information, and ideas.

20
00:01:58,783 --> 00:02:00,397
Let us pause and talk.

21
00:02:00,897 --> 00:02:06,888
What is one task Claude could take off your plate this week? And what is one thing you would never paste into it?

22
00:02:15,288 --> 00:02:17,622
Now, your concerns, answered.

23
00:02:18,122 --> 00:02:21,837
Accuracy. Claude can sound confident and still be wrong.

24
00:02:22,337 --> 00:02:29,268
It makes what you already know better. It does not replace your judgment, so spot-check names, numbers and claims.

25
00:02:29,768 --> 00:02:33,437
Losing our human touch? Claude drafts, and you decide.

26
00:02:33,937 --> 00:02:41,019
Our voice and our relationships set us apart. The clearer the guidance and examples you give, the more it sounds like us.

27
00:02:41,519 --> 00:02:46,081
How much to share? Share the situation, not the sensitive details.

28
00:02:46,581 --> 00:02:53,164
Swap real names for placeholders like Client A, and give plenty of context about the task and the tone.

29
00:02:53,664 --> 00:02:57,217
Like any new hire, Claude does best with structure.

30
00:02:57,717 --> 00:03:07,446
Give it clear guidelines, spot-check its work, and fine-tune over time. Messy processes only get messy faster, so structure first, then test.

31
00:03:07,946 --> 00:03:12,938
And data breaches? No tool is risk free, so we protect in layers.

32
00:03:13,438 --> 00:03:22,726
Approved tools, strong unique passwords with two-step login, the traffic light rules, and speaking up right away if something sensitive is shared by mistake.

33
00:03:24,126 --> 00:03:26,135
So here is the view from the summit.

34
00:03:26,635 --> 00:03:33,380
Protect what matters. Verify what it gives you. Stay human. And guide Claude like a new team member.

35
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:41,891
Claude is here to support your judgment, not replace it. Thank you for asking honest questions, because that is what makes this team strong.

36
00:03:42,391 --> 00:03:46,002
Keep the questions coming, and let us go build something great.
